### 8. Markdown parsing: `MarkdownReader::document`

Defined in `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs:57-72`:

```rust
impl Reader for MarkdownReader {
    fn document(&self, content: &str, markdown_options: &MarkdownOptions) -> Document {
        let effective = if markdown_options.bare_frontmatter {
            wrap_bare_frontmatter(content)
        } else {
            Cow::Borrowed(content)
        };

        let mut reader = MarkdownEventsReader::new_with_options(markdown_options);
        reader.read(&effective);

        Document {
            blocks: reader.blocks(),
            metadata: reader.metadata(),
        }
    }
}
```

This may call `wrap_bare_frontmatter` if configured:

```rust
if markdown_options.bare_frontmatter {
    wrap_bare_frontmatter(content)
}
```

`wrap_bare_frontmatter` only wraps leading bare front matter when content starts with `title: ` and is not already fenced with `---`.

Metadata comes from:

```rust
reader.metadata()
```

Functions involved:

1. `MarkdownReader::document`
2. optionally `wrap_bare_frontmatter`
3. `MarkdownEventsReader::new_with_options`
4. `MarkdownEventsReader::read`
5. `MarkdownEventsReader::blocks`
6. `MarkdownEventsReader::metadata`

