## Filtering path in `DocumentFinder`

### 10. `FindOptions`

Defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:35-44`:

```rust
pub struct FindOptions {
    pub query: Option<String>,
    pub roots: bool,
    pub refs_to: Option<Key>,
    pub refs_from: Option<Key>,
    pub selector: Selector,
    pub limit: Option<usize>,
    pub metadata_filters: Vec<(String, String)>,
}
```

`find_command` places `args.meta` into `metadata_filters`.

---

### 11. `DocumentFinder::new`

Defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:51-53`:

```rust
pub fn new(graph: &'a Graph) -> Self {
    Self { graph }
}
```

This just stores a reference to the loaded graph.

---

### 12. `DocumentFinder::find`

Defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:55-135`.

The high-level pipeline is:

```rust
let candidate_set = if options.selector.is_empty() {
    None
} else {
    Some(options.selector.resolve(self.graph))
};

let mut results: Vec<(Key, i64)> = self
    .graph
    .keys()
    .into_iter()
    .filter_map(|key| {
        ...
    })
    .collect();

results.sort_by(...);

let total = results.len();

let results: Vec<FindResult> = if let Some(limit) = options.limit {
    results.into_iter().take(limit).map(...).collect()
} else {
    results.into_iter().map(...).collect()
};

FindOutput { ... }
```

Inside the `filter_map`, filters are applied in this order:

#### a. Selector filter

```rust
if let Some(set) = &candidate_set {
    if !set.contains(&key) {
        return None;
    }
}
```

The selector set comes from `Selector::resolve`.

#### b. Roots filter

```rust
if options.roots && !self.is_root(&key) {
    return None;
}
```

Uses:

```rust
DocumentFinder::is_root
```

which checks:

```rust
self.graph.get_block_references_to(key).is_empty()
```

#### c. `refs_to` filter

```rust
if let Some(ref target) = options.refs_to {
    if !self.references(&key, target) {
        return None;
    }
}
```

Keeps only documents that reference the target.

#### d. `refs_from` filter

```rust
if let Some(ref source) = options.refs_from {
    if !self.references(source, &key) {
        return None;
    }
}
```

Keeps only documents referenced by the source.

#### e. Metadata filter

```rust
if !options.metadata_filters.is_empty()
    && !self.metadata_matches(&key, &options.metadata_filters)
{
    return None;
}
```

This is where `--meta` is enforced.

#### f. Query/fuzzy filter

After metadata filtering:

```rust
let title = self.graph.get_key_title(&key).unwrap_or_default();
let search_text = format!("{} {}", key, title);

let score = options
    .query
    .as_ref()
    .map(|q| matcher.fuzzy_match(&search_text, q).unwrap_or(0))
    .unwrap_or(self.node_rank(&key) as i64);

if options.query.is_some() && score == 0 {
    return None;
}

Some((key, score))
```

So `--meta` combines with a query if present, but metadata filtering happens before fuzzy query rejection.

---

## Exact metadata matching logic

### 13. `DocumentFinder::metadata_matches`

Defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:253-277`:

```rust
fn metadata_matches(&self, key: &Key, filters: &[(String, String)]) -> bool {
    let raw = match self.graph.get_metadata(key) {
        Some(s) => s,
        None => return false,
    };
    let val: serde_yaml::Value = match serde_yaml::from_str(raw) {
        Ok(v) => v,
        _ => return false,
    };
    filters.iter().all(|(k, v)| {
        val.get(k.as_str())
            .and_then(|node| match node {
                serde_yaml::Value::String(s) => Some(s.as_str() == v.as_str()),
                serde_yaml::Value::Bool(b) => Some(b.to_string() == *v),
                serde_yaml::Value::Number(n) => Some(n.to_string() == *v),
                serde_yaml::Value::Sequence(items) => Some(
                    items
                        .iter()
                        .any(|i| i.as_str().map(|s| s == v.as_str()).unwrap_or(false)),
                ),
                _ => Some(false),
            })
            .unwrap_or(false)
    })
}
```

This calls:

```rust
Graph::get_metadata
```

defined in `crates/liwe/src/graph.rs:223-225`:

```rust
pub fn get_metadata(&self, key: &Key) -> Option<&str> {
    self.metadata.get(key).map(|s| s.as_str())
}
```

### Metadata matching semantics

Given:

```bash
iwe find --meta status=ready --meta category=work
```

the function requires:

```rust
status == "ready" AND category == "work"
```

because it uses:

```rust
filters.iter().all(...)
```

### Supported YAML value types

For each `(key, value)` filter:

#### String

```yaml
status: ready
```

matches:

```bash
--meta status=ready
```

Exact string equality.

#### Bool

```yaml
published: true
```

matches:

```bash
--meta published=true
```

Because the bool is converted with `b.to_string()`.

Rust bool stringification produces lowercase `"true"` / `"false"`.

#### Number

```yaml
priority: 3
```

matches:

```bash
--meta priority=3
```

The YAML number is converted with `n.to_string()`.

#### Sequence

```yaml
tags:
  - rust
  - iwe
```

matches:

```bash
--meta tags=rust
```

But only string sequence items match, because sequence logic uses:

```rust
i.as_str().map(|s| s == v.as_str()).unwrap_or(false)
```

So this matches:

```yaml
tags:
  - rust
```

but numeric or boolean sequence items are not converted the way top-level number/bool values are.

### Non-matches

A document is excluded if:

- it has no metadata
- metadata cannot be parsed as YAML by `serde_yaml::from_str`
- the requested field is missing
- the field is not one of:
  - string
  - bool
  - number
  - sequence
- the field is a mapping/object
- the field is null
- sequence exists but no string item equals the requested value
- any one of multiple `--meta` filters fails

There is no nested path lookup. For example, this will not traverse `owner.name`:

```yaml
owner:
  name: dg
```

```bash
iwe find --meta owner.name=dg
```

It looks for a literal top-level key named `"owner.name"`.

---

## Result set construction after metadata filtering

After the filters have admitted a document, `DocumentFinder::find` assigns a score:

- If there is a query: fuzzy score against `"key title"`.
- If there is no query: rank from `DocumentFinder::node_rank`.

`node_rank` is defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:171-174`:

```rust
fn node_rank(&self, key: &Key) -> usize {
    self.graph.get_inline_references_to(key).len()
        + self.graph.get_block_references_to(key).len()
}
```

Results are sorted at `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:111`:

```rust
results.sort_by(|a, b| b.1.cmp(&a.1).then_with(|| a.0.cmp(&b.0)));
```

So:

1. Higher score first.
2. Ties by key ascending.

Then:

```rust
let total = results.len();
```

This `total` is after all filtering, including metadata.

Then optional limit is applied:

```rust
.take(limit)
```

Each remaining key becomes a `FindResult` through:

```rust
self.build_result(&key)
```

`build_result` is defined in `crates/liwe/src/find.rs:137-152` and fills in:

- key
- title
- display title
- root status
- incoming ref count
- outgoing ref count
- parent document info

Important: metadata itself is **not** included in `FindResult`; it is only used for filtering.

